                <pb facs="0898" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/3195: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-09-18T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                                1923—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 18—5:17
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>315. Asiatic News Agency telegraphs following from Mukden published in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Peking Leader</hi> of today: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“As a result of Doctor Schurman’s visit to Mukden and Harbin, General
                            Chang Tso-lin has issued instructions to General Chu Chin-Ian, chief of
                            the zone of the Chinese Eastern Railway, ordering the postponement of
                            the taking over of the land department until the problem has been fully
                            discussed by the members of the board of directors of the Chinese
                            Eastern Railway, the foreign consuls and the Chinese authorities.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
